  "reason": "Evidence: RNA-only with multi-profile + avgpool + PCA n2000 (config_002, acc=0.591) is the strongest configuration so far, and image-only ResNet50 single-profile (config_010, acc=0.208) is very weak. The central unresolved question is whether combining the strong RNA signal with image features in a multimodal setting can surpass the best RNA-only result. Question tested: Does concatenating ResNet50 image features with the proven-best RNA multi-profile/avgpool setup (config_002) yield a meaningful accuracy gain over 0.591, or does the weak image signal fail to contribute? Why this is the best next experiment: It is the direct multimodal extension of our strongest unimodal result, directly addresses the study's core hypothesis (multimodal > unimodal), and the outcome will sharply reduce uncertainty for the entire remaining multimodal branch—either confirming a promising fusion direction to exploit or indicating that image features are uninformative here, allowing us to focus budget on RNA encoder and aggregation choices."
